---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import "../../styles/global.css";
---

<Layout
	title="Distance Formula | Coordinate Geometry | Class 10 | The Concepts Adda"
	description="Learn the Distance Formula d = √[(x₂ - x₁)² + (y₂ - y₁)²], distance from origin, and collinearity test for Class 10 NCERT Mathematics."
>
	<main class="lesson-page">
		<div class="lesson-container">
			<a href="/coordinate-geometry" class="back-link">
				<span class="back-arrow">←</span>
				<span>Back to Coordinate Geometry</span>
			</a>

			<!-- LESSON HEADER -->
			<section class="lesson-header">
				<div class="lesson-number">01</div>
				<div class="lesson-header-copy">
					<div class="lesson-label">LESSON 01 · CLASS 10 MATHEMATICS (NCERT)</div>
					<h1>Distance Formula & <span>Applications</span></h1>
					<p>
						Understand how to calculate the distance between any two points in a Cartesian plane using Pythagoras Theorem.
					</p>
				</div>
			</section>

			<!-- CONTENT LAYOUT -->
			<section class="content-layout">
				<article class="lesson-content">

					<!-- 01 · THE FORMULA -->
					<div class="topic-label">01 · THE FORMULA</div>
					<h2>Distance Between Two Points</h2>
					<p>
						The distance <em>d</em> between two points <strong>P(x₁, y₁)</strong> and <strong>Q(x₂, y₂)</strong> in the Cartesian plane is given by:
					</p>

					<div class="formula-box">
						<strong>d = √[ (x₂ - x₁)² + (y₂ - y₁)² ]</strong>
						<span>derived directly using Pythagoras Theorem in right-angled △PTQ!</span>
					</div>

					<div class="idea-box">
						<div class="idea-icon">💡</div>
						<div class="idea-content">
							<strong>Distance from the Origin (0, 0)</strong>
							<p>
								The distance of a point <strong>P(x, y)</strong> from the origin <strong>O(0, 0)</strong> is:
								<br/>
								<strong>OP = √(x² + y²)</strong>
							</p>
						</div>
					</div>

					<!-- 02 · APPLICATIONS OF DISTANCE FORMULA -->
					<div class="topic-label second-label">02 · APPLICATIONS</div>
					<h2>Key Applications in Geometry</h2>

					<div class="summary-list">
						<div class="summary-item">
							<span>Collinearity</span>
							<div>
								<p><strong>Testing Collinear Points A, B, C</strong></p>
								<span style="color:#64748b; font-size:14px;">Points lie on the same straight line if <strong>AB + BC = AC</strong> (where AC is the longest segment).</span>
							</div>
						</div>
						<div class="summary-item">
							<span>Triangles</span>
							<div>
								<p><strong>Types of Triangles</strong></p>
								<span style="color:#64748b; font-size:14px;">Equilateral (3 sides equal), Isosceles (2 sides equal), Right-angled (AB² + BC² = AC²).</span>
							</div>
						</div>
						<div class="summary-item">
							<span>Quadrilaterals</span>
							<div>
								<p><strong>Testing Squares & Rectangles</strong></p>
								<span style="color:#64748b; font-size:14px;">Square: All 4 sides equal AND both diagonals equal. Rectangle: Opposite sides equal AND diagonals equal.</span>
							</div>
						</div>
					</div>

					<!-- 03 · SOLVED NCERT EXAMPLE -->
					<div class="topic-label second-label">03 · SOLVED EXAMPLE</div>
					<h2>Step-by-Step Problem Solving</h2>

					<div class="example-card">
						<div class="example-header">
							<span class="example-badge">EXAMPLE 1</span>
							<h3>Find the distance between P(2, 3) and Q(4, 1)</h3>
						</div>
						<div class="example-solution">
							<p>Given: x₁ = 2, y₁ = 3, x₂ = 4, y₂ = 1.</p>
							<p>Using <em>PQ = √[(x₂ - x₁)² + (y₂ - y₁)²]</em>:</p>
							<div class="calc-box">
								PQ = √[ (4 - 2)² + (1 - 3)² ]<br/>
								PQ = √[ (2)² + (-2)² ]<br/>
								PQ = √[ 4 + 4 ] = √8 = <strong>2√2 units</strong>
							</div>
						</div>
					</div>

					<!-- 04 · QUICK SUMMARY -->
					<div class="topic-label second-label">04 · QUICK SUMMARY</div>
					<h2>Key Takeaways</h2>

					<div class="summary-list">
						<div class="summary-item">
							<span>01</span>
							<p>Distance is always <strong>non-negative</strong> (d ≥ 0).</p>
						</div>
						<div class="summary-item">
							<span>02</span>
							<p>Distance from origin (0, 0) is <strong>√(x² + y²)</strong>.</p>
						</div>
						<div class="summary-item">
							<span>03</span>
							<p>Order does not matter because <strong>(x₂ - x₁)² = (x₁ - x₂)²</strong>.</p>
						</div>
					</div>

					<!-- LESSON NAVIGATION -->
					<div class="lesson-navigation">
						<a href="/coordinate-geometry" class="previous-lesson">
							<span>←</span>
							<div>
								<small>OVERVIEW</small>
								<strong>Chapter Overview</strong>
							</div>
						</a>

						<a href="/coordinate-geometry/section-formula" class="next-lesson">
							<div>
								<small>NEXT LESSON</small>
								<strong>Section Formula</strong>
							</div>
							<span>→</span>
						</a>
					</div>
				</article>

				<!-- SIDEBAR -->
				<aside class="lesson-sidebar">
					<div class="sidebar-card">
						<div class="sidebar-title">COORDINATE GEOMETRY</div>
						<div class="progress-text">Lesson 01 of 04</div>
						<div class="progress-bar">
							<div style="width: 25%;"></div>
						</div>

						<div class="sidebar-lessons">
							<a href="/coordinate-geometry/distance-formula" class="sidebar-lesson active">
								<span>01</span>
								<div>
									<strong>Distance Formula</strong>
									<small>Formula d = √[(x₂-x₁)² + (y₂-y₁)²]</small>
								</div>
							</a>

							<a href="/coordinate-geometry/section-formula" class="sidebar-lesson">
								<span>02</span>
								<div>
									<strong>Section Formula</strong>
									<small>Internal division & mid-point</small>
								</div>
							</a>

							<a href="/coordinate-geometry/applications-and-practice" class="sidebar-lesson">
								<span>03</span>
								<div>
									<strong>Trisection & Practice</strong>
									<small>NCERT trisection & centroid</small>
								</div>
							</a>

							<a href="/coordinate-geometry/pyqs" class="sidebar-lesson">
								<span>04</span>
								<div>
									<strong>Previous Year PYQs</strong>
									<small>CBSE 2020-2024 practice set</small>
								</div>
							</a>
						</div>
					</div>
				</aside>
			</section>
		</div>
	</main>

	<style>
